1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:06,473
Meet AI Blind Assistant, an Android app that turns object observations and printed text into spoken

2
00:00:06,473 --> 00:00:06,856
information.

3
00:00:07,096 --> 00:00:08,714
Let's follow a user's journey.

4
00:00:10,350 --> 00:00:13,888
From Home, the user opens Mobile Mode or chooses another feature.

5
00:00:14,128 --> 00:00:18,902
Large labelled controls expose the assistance status, while TalkBack support and on-demand

6
00:00:18,902 --> 00:00:21,687
permissions make the interface easier to explore.

7
00:00:22,350 --> 00:00:26,650
Before starting, the user chooses audio, vibration, or both.

8
00:00:26,890 --> 00:00:32,213
Detection sensitivity and announcement pacing can be adjusted to reduce distracting repetition.

9
00:00:32,453 --> 00:00:37,872
Accessibility options include large text and high contrast. Preferences are saved locally.

10
00:00:42,350 --> 00:00:45,032
The user opens Mobile Mode and starts assistance.

11
00:00:45,272 --> 00:00:51,302
The bundled object detector runs on the phone. Its alert policy selects relevant object names and

12
00:00:51,302 --> 00:00:54,317
relative directions for offline speech and finite vibration.

13
00:00:54,557 --> 00:01:00,753
The user can pause, resume, or stop. Visual risk is estimated; this is not exact distance

14
00:01:00,753 --> 00:01:01,140
measurement.

15
00:01:06,350 --> 00:01:12,267
To read print, the user opens Scan Document from Modes, aims at the page, and chooses Scan when

16
00:01:12,267 --> 00:01:12,596
ready.

17
00:01:12,836 --> 00:01:16,393
Local text recognition extracts the words for the spoken reader.

18
00:01:16,633 --> 00:01:21,788
The demonstration uses synthetic print. Camera images are never sent to an AI provider.

19
00:01:25,350 --> 00:01:28,551
After scanning, the reader can speak the document aloud.

20
00:01:28,791 --> 00:01:34,933
The user can pause, repeat, move between reading lines, spell words, and change reading speed.

21
00:01:35,173 --> 00:01:38,949
Scan Again returns to framing and waits for another explicit scan.

22
00:01:39,189 --> 00:01:43,864
Ask AI first creates an editable text draft; sending it is a separate choice.

23
00:01:47,350 --> 00:01:53,456
For hands-free operation, the open app supports Hey Vision AI and local commands for navigation,

24
00:01:53,456 --> 00:01:55,084
settings, and reader controls.

25
00:01:55,324 --> 00:01:57,146
Typed commands offer another route.

26
00:01:57,386 --> 00:02:02,319
These approved actions execute on the phone. Say goodbye to end the active command session.

27
00:02:05,350 --> 00:02:10,111
The optional wearable uses a Raspberry Pi camera on a private network or phone hotspot.

28
00:02:10,351 --> 00:02:14,615
The user discovers the device, establishes trust, and connects to start.

29
00:02:14,855 --> 00:02:19,959
The Pi detects locally and sends compact alerts for phone speech. Physical hardware acceptance

30
00:02:19,959 --> 00:02:20,688
remains pending.

31
00:02:21,350 --> 00:02:25,900
Smart AI adds general questions through an explicitly paired laptop running local Ollama.

32
00:02:26,140 --> 00:02:30,279
An owner-enabled Gemini option accepts text only, with local fallback.

33
00:02:30,519 --> 00:02:36,011
Pairing is optional: object awareness, document reading, and local app controls remain independent

34
00:02:36,011 --> 00:02:37,701
of this conversation service.

35
00:02:38,350 --> 00:02:43,458
The journey is simple: open, personalize, detect or read, then pause or stop when finished.

36
00:02:43,698 --> 00:02:49,041
AI Blind Assistant supplements a white cane, guide dog, and user judgment. It never guarantees a

37
00:02:49,041 --> 00:02:49,709
clear path.
